{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269c8b92c3e2fe53b028b9c6a0f503b752e9c903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1.0025)^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> is evaluated correct to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> decimal places, then the digit in the fifth decimal place is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a391e0d5a5dba36bda43859fa411e9c2832f64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }5\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269c8b92c3e2fe53b028b9c6a0f503b752e9c903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1.0025)^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0ba9780f5d757f7280f4d5b41772987d756aa69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+\\tfrac{25}{10^4})^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"85\" height=\"23\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Binomial_Theorem\" title=\"Binomial Theorem\">Binomial Theorem</a>, we know that this expression equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64ce9edfe07cd470b8195af0e5f7b5fcc3c87b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+ \\tbinom{10}1\\cdot\\tfrac{25}{10^4}+\\tbinom{10}2\\cdot\\tfrac{25^2}{10^8}+\\tbinom{10}3\\cdot\\tfrac{25^3}{10^{12}}+\\cdots+(\\tfrac{25}{10^4})^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"400\" height=\"26\" />. We are looking for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c60e61352a39cd1f835d0d2aad461b94ef7b7dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1{10^5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" /> term (the fifth decimal digit), so we can disregard the first two terms, because they will not affect our final result. Thus, we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92bbb6a5b874857e0aed7805851a2da12c1f942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tbinom{10}2\\cdot\\tfrac{25^2}{10^8}+\\tbinom{10}3\\cdot\\tfrac{25^3}{10^{12}}+\\cdots = \\tfrac{45\\cdot25^2}{10^8}+\\tfrac{120\\cdot25^3}{10^{12}}+\\cdots = \\tfrac{28,125}{10^8}+\\tfrac{1,875,000}{10^{12}}+\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"576\" height=\"26\" />. The first term here has a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c60e61352a39cd1f835d0d2aad461b94ef7b7dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1{10^5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" /> term of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the second term does not contribute to the fifth decimal place, because it does not have enough digits in the numerator. So, we can disregard the subsequent terms, because they will not have enough digits either. Thus, the fifth digit of the expansion is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129c1c4cbf3d35dbd549e42c49762617b1b73022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.